# The direct dependencies of `tools/screenshots/capture.py`, by name. Versions live in
# `requirements-screenshots.txt`, for the reason its two counterparts give.
#
# The runtime set is here because the capture serves the real app: `capture.py` imports
# `app.main` and runs it under uvicorn, so this tool needs every artefact the image has, and
# needs it to be the *same* artefact -- a picture taken against a different `starlette` is a
# picture of a different dashboard. `tests/test_dependency_lock.py` holds all three locks to
# that.
#
# `playwright` and `pillow` were the last third-party code this repository took by bare name
# (#108). They were left out of #104 because this command is rarer than a build and a
# maintainer rather than a stranger runs it -- but it runs on the host that holds both live
# tokens, as that person, with nothing bounding where it can connect, so a malicious release
# of either is import-time code there. They are fixed by content now like everything else.
#
# What this file cannot fix is the three browser archives `playwright install chromium`
# downloads afterwards. `tools/screenshots/README.md` says what that leaves open and why.

-r requirements.in

pillow
playwright
